    "question": "A bathroom has 10 6 inch tiles along its width and 20 6 inch tiles along its length.  What is the square footage of the bathroom?",
    "gold": "50",
    "answer": "There are 10 tiles that are 6 inches long running the width of the bathroom so it is 10*6 = <<10*6=60>>60 inches long\nThere are 12 inches in a foot and it’s 60 inches wide so it is 60/12 = 5 feet wide\nThere are 20 tiles that are 6 inches long running the length of the bathroom so it’s 20*6 = <<20*6=120>>120 inches long\nThere are 12 inches in a foot and it’s 120 inches long so it is 120/12 = <<120/12=10>>10 feet wide\nThe square footage is l x w so the bathroom has 10*5 = <<10*5=50>>50 sq feet\n#### 50"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the square footage of the bathroom, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the width of the bathroom in inches.\n2. Calculate the length of the bathroom in inches.\n3. Convert the width and length from inches to feet.\n4. Calculate the area of the bathroom in square feet.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the width of the bathroom in inches.**\n\nThe width of the bathroom is given as 10 tiles, and each tile is 6 inches wide. Therefore, the width in inches is:\n\\[ 10 \\times 6 = 60 \\text{ inches} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the length of the bathroom in inches.**\n\nThe length of the bathroom is given as 20 tiles, and each tile is 6 inches long. Therefore, the length in inches is:\n\\[ 20 \\times 6 = 120 \\text{ inches} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert the width and length from inches to feet.**\n\nSince there are 12 inches in a foot, we convert the width and length to feet:\n\\[ \\text{Width in feet} = \\frac{60}{12} = 5 \\text{ feet} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Length in feet} = \\frac{120}{12} = 10 \\text{ feet} \\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the area of the bathroom in square feet.**\n\nThe area of a rectangle is given by the product of its length and width. Therefore, the area of the bathroom is:\n\\[ 5 \\times 10 = 50 \\text{ square feet} \\]\n\nThus, the square footage of the bathroom is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
